    "title": {
      "en": "Taiga or Tundra Bean Goose?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Look at the bill and the neck. A Taiga Bean Goose is tall, with a long neck and a long, deep bill with a long orange band, and it looks rather flat-headed. A Tundra Bean Goose is stocky and short-necked, with a short, mostly black bill with a thin orange band. The Tundra is by far the commoner in the Netherlands and Germany."
    }
